Yes, at least in the Android browser described here you can view the page source by using JavaScript in the address bar:

javascript: alert(document.getElementsByTagName('html')[0].innerHTML);

This is a workaround to display the HTML source. The provided information does not say whether a built-in “view source” option exists in any browser.

The supported method shown is to write the raw images directly, not to format first:

package_extract_file("aboot.img", "/dev/block/mmcblk0p5");
package_extract_file("modem.img", "/dev/block/mmcblk0p1");

This suggests formatting isn’t needed for raw image flashing. If you’re trying to format a flash drive specifically, the provided material doesn’t explain that process. It only covers copying raw partition images to block devices.
